Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?Tier=201=20=C2=B7=20seven=20quick-win=20polish?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20fixes=20for=20the=20DIO=20walkthrough?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Q1 · Full names replace initials in USERS.name (10 users)
     'E. Hughes' -> 'Emma Hughes' etc. Cascades to every nav-user chip
     and greeting across the app.

Q2 · User-switch stability + defensive re-mount
     shared_user_switch.js toggleMenu now re-mounts the dropdown on open
     (with a force flag) so users are never stuck if the initial mount
     ran before USERS was defined. Navigation now uses location.assign()
     for hard redirects.

Q3 · DIO 'Requests' & 'Cases' top-nav tabs land on their widgets
     dio.html load-handler now honours window.location.hash after
     render so /dio.html#w-requests + #w-portfolio scroll to their
     widgets. Fixes the 'nothing happens' feel when Emma clicks the
     Requests or Cases tabs.

Q4 · Weather-page airports default to Tier 1 (capital-city hubs)
     evidence-weather.html gains a Show filter: default 'Capitals only'
     (Tier 1) makes the list recognisable at first glance; user can
     toggle to 'All 63 airports' for full view. Page-sub copy updated.

Q5 · Evidence-page corner user chip now dynamic (was hardcoded SB)
     Injected a small sync script into 8 evidence-*.html pages that
     reads active user on load and updates gn-av + gn-username.

Q6 · Removed 'evidence collection pipeline health' widget from Sarah
     Booth's dashboard (defendable_evidence_status_widget) — unclear
     which team it addressed and mixed DIO/solicitor concerns.

Q7 · Confusing 'Repository ->' / 'Evidence Repository ->' cross-links
     rewritten to plain wording ('Open documents repository',
     'View attached evidence') in case_shell.js.

Cache-bust: shared_data.js / shared_user_switch.js / case_shell.js
promoted to s10a across every affected HTML.
